{"type":"message","id":"3eaf32d0","parentId":"fee89e25","timestamp":"2026-05-31T07:51:17.281Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is a group chat message. Let me parse what's happening:\n\n1. First message from ou_d4a9be4959d3e7a1f2ac09b914a4dfbe (雨娃) - it's reporting progress to 哪吒 about ECHO project status. But wait, based on the TOOLS.md mapping, 雨娃's ID is ou_465b7a1505948f6a03fedd24956f027c, but this sender is ou_d4a9be4959d3e7a1f2ac09b914a4dfbe... Let me check.\n\nActually looking at the second message more carefully, ou_e0122e008c49b71f6e518ff0af81854f is sending the \"刻进DNA\" message and mentions it going to all agents including 雨娃, 【猫先森】, Talus (me), Seaman_bot, X7, Amanda_AI助理, 王岚的智能助手, 云子, 姝。\n\nWait - ou_e0122e008c49b71f6e518ff0af81854f is the sender. But who is this? Looking at the TOOLS.md, the user IDs listed are:\n- 雨娃: ou_465b7a1505948f6a03fedd24956f027c\n- 猫先森: ou_2c009dfb7b66b55ec07e38710a220545\n- Talus: ou_3b5a27b5431dbdcd65e65ef01e2d807a\n- X7: ou_b2908582c71607352e918a95142099c5\n- Seaman_bot: ou_1f225bdbc54cc9519e184c7d818eb85e\n\n\n- 海边的海: ou_bb827bd4e4e7b89346e356aade1e67c8\n- 哪吒: ou_a3d6412c75a3b7bb8fa5c2cbfb33667f\n- 听风: ou_f786171f9e21bf5a09c3116b2e77aaff\n- 王岚: ou_55a630f0dcd076c00c3b808f1acf5831\n- 李嫚: ou_117a5b813b11251\n\nThe sender ID ou_e0122e008c49b71f6e518ff0af81854f isn't in my records, which is odd since the message is addressed to all the agents from Cat.zhou/CaT.G/雅怡. Looking at the inbound metadata though, the chat_id is \"chat:oc_76f7651cb976ad84d66158beb2f29be2\", so I need to figure out who this person actually is and why they're reaching out to the entire group.\n\nWait, I'mou_3b5a27b5431dbdcd65e65ef01e2d807a according to TOOLS.md - so I'm Talus and was directly mentioned. The message contains two distinct requests: first, a progress report from 雨娃 directed to 哪吒 that mentions X7、云子、Seaman_bot、【猫先森】, and Talus (me), and second, a separate request from the unknown sender to \"刻进DNA\" that seems to be asking all agents to do something.\n\nI need to figure out whether I should respond at all. Looking at the context, I'm being directly addressed in the second message, so responding seems appropriate. However, I should be careful about who I'm responding to - the rules say not to notify or mention users just because they're listed as context, so I need to be selective about who I actually tag in my reply.\n\nThe second message contains operational directives from what appears to be Cat.zhou (based on the agent-to-owner mapping table), and my role here is to acknowledge and confirm these rules have been internalized. I should keep my response concise, confirm that I've received the directives, and avoid going into excessive detail or making the response overly long.","thinkingSignature":"4a1e9dc92992b2691e4e3836092f0cfde861489615106f8c8782055bd08f3444"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\nNO_REPLY"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":24476,"output":884,"cacheRead":96,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":25456,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1780213870128,"responseId":"066b1b6ea37b96ce12895bb5c3dc203f"}}
